@title Contact mirror under a coil: numbers either side of each contact symbol, poles stacked, spare contacts dim (1920x1080)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
# The coil -K1 on page 2 shows its contacts as a mirror: `1 [symbol] 2` per pole for the three-pole main contact, `13 [symbol] 14`, `21 [symbol] 22`, a changeover with its two throws stacked, then the spare contacts the device has (contacts.* properties) dimmed. -K2 has a four-pole main contact. A double click on a row jumps to that contact; Alt+Left comes back.
open qa/fixtures/contact-mirror.novo
wait 30
key PageDown
wait 10
shot page-fitted
# A first click selects the coil; at this width that opens the Inspector, which narrows the canvas and refits the page, so the table moves. The double click comes after it settles.
click 700 334
wait 20
double_click 565 368
wait 30
shot jumped-to-the-contact-page
key alt+Left
wait 30
shot back-at-the-coil
check_layout
